In-Reply-To: <FqTR7yc8uzU.CbAOS2qnAAAJ@dartr.groups.google.com>
References: <FqTR7yc8uzU.CbAOS2qnAAAJ@dartr.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/dartr/c/FqTR7yc8uzU/m/C0C9UkuoAAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi Yasuto,

SNPs with more than two alleles are filtered out when you read/convert your data into dartR, ie. genlight objects only store bi-allelic data.

Cheers,
Luis

